  "b4_text_layer_sanitized": "50\nNone of the provided chapters in the list are relevant to the question about lenses and their focal lengths, which i…\nTwo thin lenses are of same focal lengths (f), but one is convex and the other one is concave. When\nthey are placed in contact with each other, the equivalent focal length of the combination will be :\n(1)\nZero\n(2)\nf/4\n(3)\nf/2\n(4)\nInfinite\n\n1\n​ +\nf\n​1\n1\n​\nf\n​2\n1\nf\n​ =\n1\nf\nf\n​ =\n2\n−f\n​ =\nF\n1\n​ +\nf\n1\n​ =\n−f\n1\n0 ⇒F = ∞\n",
